infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title During a partition: CP vs AP — one binary choice
  desc P is mandatory. Each isolated side either stays correct or stays responsive — never both.
  compares
    - label CP — choose Consistency
      children
        - label Return an error (HTTP 503)
          desc Deny the request so no stale or conflicting value is ever read or written. Correctness is absolute.
        - label Guarantees linearizability
          desc A global real-time order of all ops; a read always sees the latest committed write.
        - label etcd, Consul, Spanner, MongoDB (default)
          desc Raft minority rejects writes; primary steps down to preserve truth.
    - label AP — choose Availability
      children
        - label Answer with local data
          desc Accept the request and serve possibly-stale state on both sides. Responsiveness is absolute.
        - label Pays the conflict-resolution tax
          desc Divergent writes must reconcile on heal; naive Last-Write-Wins can silently drop a customer write.
        - label Cassandra, DynamoDB
          desc Replicas accept writes independently; CRDTs or vector clocks add complexity to repair safely.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
